{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_ncv", "label": "ncv NetCDF Viewer", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/SanjeevBashyal/ncv.git", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A PyQt6 desktop viewer combining dimension selection, pyqtgraph plots, an optional Cartopy map view, and an array/metadata table in one application; explicitly a viewer, not an editor or export tool."}, {"id": "readme_scatter_line_tab", "label": "Scatter/Line Tab", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Scatter/Line tab", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Y and Y2 get fully independent axes, limits and styling so two series on different scales share one X axis; X is optional and falls back to the sample index."}, {"id": "readme_contour_tab", "label": "Contour Tab", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Contour tab", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A 2D Z slice is drawn as a heat map with one image cell per grid cell rather than interpolated contour lines, keeping the display faithful to the source grid; zlim clips as well as scales the color range."}, {"id": "readme_map_tab", "label": "Map Tab", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Map tab", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Requires the map/full extra; uses Cartopy only for projection maths and Natural Earth features while pyqtgraph does the drawing. Missing coordinates fall back to a generated regular global lon/lat grid from the data shape."}, {"id": "readme_matrix_tab", "label": "Matrix and Metadata Tab", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Matrix tab", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A read-only array table doubling as the metadata browser: with no Z selected it shows dataset dimensions/variables/groups/attributes, with Z it shows that variable's metadata. It refuses to reshape data implicitly when more than two dimensions remain, asking for more selection instead."}, {"id": "readme_time_controls", "label": "Shared Time Navigation Controls", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Time controls", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Map and Matrix share one time-navigation widget set active only when the selected variable carries the detected time dimension; slider, dimension selector, displayed frame and Time: label stay synchronized, and boundary mode (once/repeat/reflect) decides animation behavior at the ends."}, {"id": "readme_dimension_selection", "label": "Dimension Retain/Index/Reduce Selection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Basic workflow", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One uniform selector grammar covers every tab: `all` retains a dimension, a zero-based integer picks an element, and mean/std/min/max/ptp/sum/median/var reduce it, so high-dimensional variables are explicitly narrowed to the dimensionality each view requires."}, {"id": "readme_session_sharing", "label": "Shared Session and New Window", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Basic workflow", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "New Window opens another viewer backed by the same session so several views of one dataset stay in sync; opening a file in any of those windows refreshes every window sharing the session."}, {"id": "readme_missing_data_handling", "label": "Missing-Data Handling", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "File-reading behavior", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Missing values combine the --miss command-line value, _FillValue, missing_value, and the type's default NetCDF fill value, so metadata-declared sentinels and ad-hoc ones are masked together; NaN and missing render as blank table cells."}, {"id": "readme_netcdf4_backend", "label": "netCDF4 Default Reading Backend", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "File-reading behavior", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Supports either one file (groups allowed) or multiple files without groups; group names and multi-file identifiers appear in the variable list."}, {"id": "readme_xarray_backend", "label": "xarray Reading Path", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "File-reading behavior", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Selected with -x/--xarray; uses xarray.open_dataset for one file and open_mfdataset for many. Without xarray installed the netCDF4 reader remains and the Open xarray button is simply hidden rather than erroring."}, {"id": "readme_group_multifile_conflict", "label": "Group and Multi-File Naming Conflict Rejection", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "File-reading behavior", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Opening multiple files when one contains NetCDF groups is rejected with a clear error because group names and multi-file identifiers are two naming schemes that would be ambiguous if combined in the variable list."}, {"id": "readme_cf_time_decoding", "label": "CF-Style Time Coordinate Decoding", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Features", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Decoding CF time when possible lets datetime coordinates be used directly on plot axes and in limit fields such as `2025-01-01, 2025-12-31`."}, {"id": "readme_lon_lat_autodetection", "label": "Longitude/Latitude Auto-Selection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Features", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recognized longitude and latitude variables are chosen automatically as the Map coordinates and as the default Matrix X and Y headers, so the common geospatial case needs no manual wiring."}, {"id": "readme_limit_field_syntax", "label": "Limit Field Syntax (xlim/ylim/y2lim/zlim)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Scatter/Line tab", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One shared `min, max` or `(min, max)` grammar across the plotting tabs, where `None` on either bound independently enables automatic scaling for that side only."}, {"id": "readme_map_downsampling", "label": "Map Grid Downsampling and Full Res", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Map tab", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Large grids are downsampled by default to keep the map responsive, with `full res` as the explicit opt-in to draw every cell: interactivity is the default, fidelity the deliberate choice."}, {"id": "readme_full_variable_range", "label": "Full-Variable Range Calculation (all)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Map tab", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Initial color/value ranges may be computed from a sample of a large variable; the `all` option forces inspection of the complete variable. It is opt-in because full-variable range calculations are expensive for very large arrays."}, {"id": "readme_table_formatting", "label": "Matrix Table Formatting and Flipping", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Matrix tab", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cell values and coordinate headers carry independent fixed-point/scientific formats with 0-8 decimals; flipping top-to-bottom or left-to-right keeps data and headers synchronized, and coordinate-size mismatches fall back to zero-based source indices rather than misaligning."}, {"id": "readme_qt_designer_forms", "label": "Qt Designer Forms in ncv/ui", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Editing the interface with Qt Designer", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "main_window.ui, scatter_panel.ui, contour_panel.ui, map_panel.ui, map_unavailable.ui and matrix_panel.ui are loaded at runtime with PyQt6.uic.loadUi; pyqtgraph widgets, dimension selectors and the Matrix model are attached to the loaded forms afterwards, so Designer never needs to know about them."}, {"id": "readme_widget_object_name_contract", "label": "Widget Object Name Contract", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Editing the interface with Qt Designer", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Because forms are loaded at runtime, widget object names are the only contract between the .ui files and their Python controllers; renaming or removing an object requires updating its Python references and tests in the same change or it fails only at runtime."}, {"id": "readme_python_launcher", "label": "Python Launcher ncv()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Python launcher", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "`from ncv import ncv` gives the same entry point as the console script and `python3 -m ncv`, accepting a path or list of paths plus miss and usex arguments mirroring --miss and --xarray."}, {"id": "readme_optional_extras", "label": "Optional Install Extras", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Requirements", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "map, xarray, full and test extras sit on a core of netCDF4, NumPy, PyQt6 and pyqtgraph, so the heavy geospatial and dask-adjacent stacks are opt-in and the core install stays small."}, {"id": "readme_pyqtgraph_rendering", "label": "pyqtgraph Rendering and Export", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Scatter/Line tab", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All plotting tabs rely on pyqtgraph for pan, zoom and the right-click export menu; image export comes free from pyqtgraph, which is why there is no separate data-export command."}, {"id": "readme_cli_arguments", "label": "Command-Line Interface", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Command-line reference", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "`ncv [-h] [-m missing_value] [-x] [netcdf_file ...]` takes zero or more files so the app can also start empty and open files from the interface."}, {"id": "readme_ncv_app_py", "label": "ncv/app.py Module Responsibility", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Editing the interface with Qt Designer", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Main window, tabs, file dialogs and shared windows."}, {"id": "readme_ncv_session_py", "label": "ncv/session.py Module Responsibility", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Editing the interface with Qt Designer", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "File lifecycle and session state."}, {"id": "readme_ncv_dimensions_py", "label": "ncv/dimensions.py Module Responsibility", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Editing the interface with Qt Designer", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Toolkit-neutral dimension selector specifications."}, {"id": "readme_ncv_ncvcommon_py", "label": "ncv/ncvcommon.py Module Responsibility", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Editing the interface with Qt Designer", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shared Qt panel and time-control behavior."}, {"id": "readme_ncv_ncvscatter_py", "label": "ncv/ncvscatter.py Module Responsibility", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Editing the interface with Qt Designer", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scatter/Line tab."}, {"id": "readme_ncv_ncvcontour_py", "label": "ncv/ncvcontour.py Module Responsibility", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Editing the interface with Qt Designer", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Contour tab."}, {"id": "readme_ncv_ncvmap_py", "label": "ncv/ncvmap.py Module Responsibility", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Editing the interface with Qt Designer", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Map tab (pyqtgraph rendering, Cartopy projections) and the optional-Cartopy fallback panel."}, {"id": "readme_ncv_ncvmatrix_py", "label": "ncv/ncvmatrix.py Module Responsibility", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Editing the interface with Qt Designer", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Matrix table and metadata tab."}], "edges": [{"source": "readme_ncv", "target": "readme_scatter_line_tab", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Features", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_ncv", "target": "readme_contour_tab", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Features", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_ncv", "target": "readme_map_tab", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Features", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_ncv", "target": "readme_matrix_tab", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Features", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_ncv", "target": "readme_cli_arguments", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Command-line reference", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_ncv", "target": "readme_optional_extras", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Requirements", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_python_launcher", "target": "readme_cli_arguments", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Python launcher", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_cli_arguments", "target": "readme_missing_data_handling", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Command-line reference", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_cli_arguments", "target": "readme_xarray_backend", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Command-line refe